BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Exhibit | Divestment Now! Student Activism and the Anti-Apartheid 
 Movement at UC Berkeley — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261021T000000
DTSTAMP:20261022T214018Z
UID:fad59b68dd8a41798b445479ccf0@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Exhibits\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:In 1985\, UC Berkeley students\, with support from faculty\, s
 taff\, and labor unions\, transformed the campus into the heart of a power
 ful anti-apartheid divestment campaign. They organized rallies\, teach-ins
 \, and shantytown encampments to protest the university’s financial ties
  to companies profiting from South Africa’s system of racial segregation
 .\nCategory: Exhibits\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/live/
 events/309073-exhibit-divestment-now-student-activism-and-the-anti-
LOCATION:The Rowell Exhibition Cases\, Doe Library\, 2nd floor\, The Rowel
 l Exhibition Cases\, Doe Library\, 2nd floor
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/live/events/309073-exhibit-divestment-now-
 student-activism-and-the-anti-
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
