SUMMARY:Film Screening: Sunday Beauty Queen — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261022T160000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261022T173000
DTSTAMP:20261022T214018Z
UID:6e6054925e4601c3389d9fc65fda@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a screening of the film Sunday Beauty Queen . Baby
  Ruth Villarama’s documentary intimately explores the work and social li
 ves of five Overseas Filipino Workers (OFWs) working in Hong Kong through 
 the lens of community beauty pageants run by and for OFWs. “We are not j
 ust domestic helpers. Even if people look down at what we do\, [ Sunday Be
 auty Queen ] is an opportunity for us to raise our voices\,” - Mylyn Jac
 obo\, one of the women profiled in the film.\nCategory: Films\nOriginal li
 sting: https://events.berkeley.edu/live/events/334486-film-screening-sunda
 y-beauty-queen
LOCATION:2521 Channing Way\, Berkeley\, CA 94720\, 2521 Channing Way\, Ber
 keley\, CA 94720
