BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Breathless — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261022T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-07:00":20261022T200000
DTSTAMP:20261022T214018Z
UID:71aeb0695a2020156a52efc68be2@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Jean-Luc Godard’s films of the 1960s are rich in intellectua
 l references\, gorgeous visuals\, and music by Michel Legrand—classicall
 y French\, in their postmodern way. But scrappy\, jazzy\, black-and-white 
 Breathless remains what Russell Merritt called “the outlaw artifact of t
 he nouvelle vague.” A very young Jean-Paul Belmondo plays the outlaw her
 o Michel Poiccard (alias Laszlo Kovacs)\, who kills a cop and hides in pla
 in sight in Paris. An even younger Jean Seberg announces herself loudly as
  an American student working for the New York Herald Tribune . “A thrill
 ing reminder of how playful Godard could be” (Ella Taylor\, Village Voic
 e ).\nCategory: Films\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPF
 A/event/328119-film-screening-breathless
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/328119-film-screening-breathl
 ess
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
